      "id": "timer-symmetry-recovery-lapse",
      "property_ref": "bounded-coordinator-recovery",
      "inspiration_ref": "timer-symmetry-liveness",
      "summary": "After the single allowed drop removes n1's message to n2, a pulse to n2 starts a competing ballot. Immediately after leadership moves to n2, a pulse to n1 can make the old leader recontest. A communicating quorum exists, but two high-priority nodes keep alternating ballot/promise evidence and the client entry does not advance to a decision within the investigation horizon.",
      "suspected_mechanism": "client-invoked [workload-invoked]: The client operation enters the replicated log through the active coordinator. -\u003e follower-silenced [message-dropped]: The only permitted fault removes the next message destined for the lower-priority voter, leaving n2 without fresh ballot evidence. -\u003e follower-pulse [temporal-fired]: The natural periodic pulse reaches n2 while it has not heard from n1, starting a higher-ballot attempt. -\u003e old-leader-promise [omnipaxos/promise-raised]: n1's promise to n2's new ballot is the public signal that the old leader has acknowledged the higher ballot. -\u003e leadership-handoff [coordinator-changed]: The coordinator observation records that leadership has moved from n1 to n2 after the new ballot is accepted. -\u003e old-leader-reclaim [temporal-fired]: A pulse to n1 after the transition is the symmetric event that can make it reclaim leadership and prevent stable decision progress.",
      "mechanism_steps": [
        {
          "milestone_id": "client-invoked",
          "kind": "workload-invoked",
          "rationale": "The client operation enters the replicated log through the active coordinator.",
          "support_refs": [
            "surface/workload",
            "dossier/contracts/append-origin-identity",
            "dossier/active-experiment/worker-priority-config"
          ]
        },
        {
          "milestone_id": "follower-silenced",
          "kind": "message-dropped",
          "rationale": "The only permitted fault removes the next message destined for the lower-priority voter, leaving n2 without fresh ballot evidence.",
          "support_refs": [
            "surface/fault-allowance",
            "dossier/contracts/produced-message-only",
            "dossier/control-semantics/stored-message-control"
          ]
        },
        {
          "milestone_id": "follower-pulse",
          "kind": "temporal-fired",
          "rationale": "The natural periodic pulse reaches n2 while it has not heard from n1, starting a higher-ballot attempt.",
          "support_refs": [
            "dossier/control-semantics/natural-periodic-pulse",
            "dossier/active-experiment/worker-priority-config",
            "surface/temporal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "milestone_id": "old-leader-promise",
          "kind": "omnipaxos/promise-raised",
          "rationale": "n1's promise to n2's new ballot is the public signal that the old leader has acknowledged the higher ballot.",
          "support_refs": [
            "surface/observations",
            "dossier/components/runtime-owned-network"
          ]
        },
        {
          "milestone_id": "leadership-handoff",
          "kind": "coordinator-changed",
